:name: mpfs-freertos-smode demo (headless)
:description: Loads the board and the simulated devices as the debug launcher does, runs the demo without a debugger and writes MMUART1 to a file.

# Normally run by 'make sim' (top-level Makefile), which also checks the
# output. By hand, with Renode started in the project root:
#
#   renode --disable-xwt --console -e "$uart_log=@/abs/path/uart1.txt; include @renode/run-demo.resc"
#
# Variables (set them before the include):
#   $uart_log   MMUART1 output file. Must be an absolute path: Renode 1.13
#               does not resolve a relative one against the working directory.
#   $elf        the program (default: the demo the top-level make builds)
#   $runtime    emulated seconds before quitting (default "3")
#
# Every other path here is relative to the working directory, so start Renode
# in the project root ($ORIGIN is not expanded inside paths in 1.13).

$elf?=@build/examples/freertos-demo/freertos-demo.elf
$runtime?="3"

using sysbus
mach create
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/polarfire-soc.repl
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/mpfs-ddr-38bit-cached-3gib.repl
include @renode/models/SpiLoopback.cs
include @renode/models/NorFlash.cs
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/mpfs-sim-peripherals.repl

# The MPFS_SPI model does not implement the SPS/CLKMODE bits or FRAMESUP and
# warns on every transfer; harmless (see renode/README.md).
logLevel 3 spi0
logLevel 3 spi1

# LoadELF uses the physical (load) addresses. Every hart starts at the
# physical reset vector, as the debug launcher does with 'set $pc'.
sysbus LoadELF $elf
e51 PC 0x08000000
u54_1 PC 0x08000000
u54_2 PC 0x08000000
u54_3 PC 0x08000000
u54_4 PC 0x08000000

mmuart1 CreateFileBackend $uart_log true

echo "run-demo: running (emulated seconds:)"
echo $runtime
emulation RunFor $runtime

echo "run-demo: spi0.flash programs, erases, ignored commands:"
spi0.flash Programs
spi0.flash Erases
spi0.flash IgnoredCommands
echo "run-demo: done"
quit
